      "text": "HTTP\n(REST, Web\nAPI,\nREstful, etc)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "G9RaG_qjMxGIOQb_sQxs-",
      "originalText": "HTTP\n(REST, Web API, REstful, etc)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EsUCeygNFrE3xUkdjjGSg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 536.5,
      "y": 225,
      "width": 616,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1152990531,
      "version": 121,
      "versionNonce": 1976945539,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794845749720,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "some code that owns some data (exclusively) and provides\nmechanisms through which that data is maintained.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "some code that owns some data (exclusively) and provides\nmechanisms through which that data is maintained.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "kK7nvrxB4zjdR4AgxiI6J",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 520.5,
      "y": 439,
      "width": 715,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a9",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1455752899,
      "version": 219,
      "versionNonce": 84891405,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794846040228,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Is the mechanism we provide to other software developers\nto do the things we want them to do to the data our service owns.\nApplicatrion Programming Interface - it's a \"UI\" for software.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Is the mechanism we provide to other software developers\nto do the things we want them to do to the data our service owns.\nApplicatrion Programming Interface - it's a \"UI\" for software.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4kkfMAcouh8OF5leDlM6E",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 517.5,
      "y": 639,
      "width": 726,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aA",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 263278371,
      "version": 483,
      "versionNonce": 1073513795,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794846554666,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HTTP is an \"application layer\" protocol\nIt defines how two applications can talk to each other.\nIt is one way to provide an API\n- The more you can stick to the \"normal\" way HTTP Apis work\n   the easier it will be for other developers to use your API.\n- HTTP is \"normative\" - has opinions about how to do things,\n   resist as much as possible making your API super \"enterprisey\".\n\nRFC 2616 basis for using HTTP (standard)\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HTTP is an \"application layer\" protocol\nIt defines how two applications can talk to each other.\nIt is one way to provide an API\n- The more you can stick to the \"normal\" way HTTP Apis work\n   the easier it will be for other developers to use your API.\n- HTTP is \"normative\" - has opinions about how to do things,\n   resist as much as possible making your API super \"enterprisey\".\n\nRFC 2616 basis for using HTTP (standard)\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
